#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_marin
msgid ""
"=====\n"
"Marin\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"AgroMarin's central installer module. Extends and customizes nearly every\n"
"functional area of Odoo for a Mexican agricultural company: accounting\n"
"(MX EDI/CFDI), sales, purchasing, inventory (reconditioning, productivity\n"
"tracking, granular permissions), manufacturing, POS, HR/payroll, partner\n"
"profiling/scoring, project management, and document management.\n"
"\n"
"See ``oca_dependencies.txt`` for required repositories.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Subsystem Overview\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"The module is organized in 8 interconnected subsystems that extend Odoo's\n"
"core functional areas:\n"
"\n"
".. code-block:: text\n"
"\n"
"                             ┌─────────────────────────────┐\n"
"                             │      PARTNER PROFILING       │\n"
"                             │ res.partner (extended)       │\n"
"                             │ res.partner.age.range        │\n"
"                             │ res.partner.tag (ext)   │\n"
"                             │ scoring -> agro_profile      │\n"
"                             └──────┬──────────────┬────────┘\n"
"                                    │              │\n"
"               ┌────────────────────▼──┐    ┌──────▼──────────────────┐\n"
"               │    SALES & TARGETS    │    │   PURCHASE CATEGORIES   │\n"
"               │ sale.order (ext)      │    │ purchase.order (ext)    │\n"
"               │ sale.target(.line)    │    │ 4 vendor category groups│\n"
"               │ sale.order.template   │    │ approval categories     │\n"
"               │ season_id (date.range)│    └─────────────────────────┘\n"
"               └────────┬──────────────┘\n"
"                        │\n"
"    ┌───────────────────▼───────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n"
"    │       WAREHOUSE & PRODUCTIVITY         │   │    MX LOCALIZATION (EDI)     │\n"
"    │ stock.picking (ext, 52 methods)        │   │ account.move (ext)           │\n"
"    │ stock.picking.type (8 user M2M)        │   │ account.move.line (ext)      │\n"
"    │ stock.move / stock.move.line (ext)     │   │ l10n_mx_edi.document (ext)   │\n"
"    │ stock.location (distance calc)         │   │ x_treatment fiscal flag      │\n"
"    │ stock.quant (custom removal)           │   │ SAT status + cancel alerts   │\n"
"    │ V1-V5 time windows                     │   │ PUE/PPD payment policy       │\n"
"    │ Zigzag / Circuit methods               │   │ BBVA bank import             │\n"
"    └───────────┬────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────┘\n"
"                │\n"
"    ┌───────────▼───────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n"
"    │    PRODUCT RECONDITIONING     │   │         POS CASH MGMT            │\n"
"    │ stock.lot (parent/child)      │   │ pos.session (ext)                │\n"
"    │ stock.quant (eligibility)     │   │ pos.config (ext)                 │\n"
"    │ stock.reconditioning.wizard   │   │ pos.order / pos.order.line (ext) │\n"
"    │ mrp.bom (reformulated type)   │   │ pos.cash.transfer.wizard         │\n"
"    │ mrp.production (auto-created) │   │ account.move (pos_session link)  │\n"
"    │ stock.warehouse (allow flag)  │   └──────────────────────────────────┘\n"
"    └───────────────────────────────┘\n"
"                                        ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n"
"                                        │         HR & PAYROLL             │\n"
"                                        │ hr.employee (MX type, POS flag)  │\n"
"                                        │ hr.payslip / hr.payslip.run      │\n"
"                                        │ hr.version (SDI, seniority)      │\n"
"                                        │ hr.job (job rank)                │\n"
"                                        └──────────────────────────────────┘\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Partner Profiling\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"Customer scoring was extracted from ``marin`` into the dedicated\n"
"``agro_profile`` module (t22384, transitional rewrite). ``marin`` no longer\n"
"computes scores or profiles and no longer owns ``res.partner.hectares.range``\n"
"or ``res.partner.profile.history``; the ``res.partner.profile`` bucket was\n"
"renamed to ``agro.profile``. ``marin`` now only *consumes* the result through\n"
"``partner.agro_profile_id`` (e.g. ``sale.target``).\n"
"\n"
"The scoring engine — UI-configurable weights over agro surfaces and EAV\n"
"attributes, percentage normalization, and a per-dimension audit trail\n"
"(``agro.profile.score``) — lives in ``agro_profile``. See that module for the\n"
"current compute chain and the migration away from the legacy tag-based engine.\n"
"\n"
"Age chain::\n"
"\n"
"    birthdate ──→ _compute_age ──→ age ──→ _compute_age_range_id ──→ age_range_id\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Warehouse Productivity\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"Measures operator efficiency during picking by comparing theoretical vs.\n"
"actual completion times. Lifecycle::\n"
"\n"
"    1. Picking confirmed/assigned\n"
"    2. action_operator_checkin()\n"
"       ├── Opens stock.picking.assign.wizard (supervisor validates)\n"
"       └── Sets operator_check_in = now()\n"
"    3. action_calculate_theoretical_times()\n"
"       ├── Reads config params (buffer, speed, seconds_per_unit)\n"
"       ├── For each move_line, calculates 5 time windows:\n"
"       │   ├── V1: Travel to pick location + buffer (first line only)\n"
"       │   ├── V2: Ascent to rack level (uses posz from stock_threed)\n"
"       │   ├── V3: Picking time (base_time * quantity)\n"
"       │   ├── V4: Descent with product\n"
"       │   └── V5: Travel to destination + buffer (last line only)\n"
"       └── Two methods:\n"
"           ├── zigzag: sequential line-by-line\n"
"           └── circuit: nearest-neighbor by XY coords\n"
"    4. action_operator_checkout()\n"
"       └── Triggers _compute_productivity_metrics\n"
"           ├── productivity_percentage = real / theoretical * 100\n"
"           └── efficiency_rating:\n"
"               ├── excellent (>= 120%)   ├── good (100-119%)\n"
"               └── average (80-99%)      └── poor (< 80%)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Product Reconditioning\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"Extends shelf life by creating a new lot from an existing one via MO::\n"
"\n"
"    stock.quant (can_be_reconditioned=True)\n"
"        └── action_open_reconditioning_wizard()\n"
"            └── stock.reconditioning.wizard\n"
"                ├── Validates: group, quant, warehouse flag, mrp access\n"
"                ├── _get_or_create_bom()  [production_type='reformulated']\n"
"                ├── _get_or_create_lot()  [new or reuse, parent_lot_id link]\n"
"                └── _create_manufacturing_order(bom, new_lot)\n"
"                    ├── Consume parent lot (manual component move)\n"
"                    ├── Produce new lot (manual finished move)\n"
"                    └── Force MO to state='done'\n"
"\n"
"Lot chain (self-referential)::\n"
"\n"
"    Original Lot A (parent_lot_id = False)\n"
"        └── Reconditioned Lot A-R1 (parent_lot_id = A)\n"
"            └── Re-reconditioned Lot A-R2 (parent_lot_id = A-R1)\n"
"\n"
"``_get_root_lot()`` walks up recursively. ``_check_parent_lot_cycle()``\n"
"validates no circular references.\n"
"\n"
"Custom removal strategy: when no strategy is defined on category or\n"
"location, default is ``refurbished + fefo + priority`` — order by\n"
"``original_expiration_date ASC, removal_date ASC, removal_priority ASC,\n"
"id``. Prioritizes reconditioned products (shorter original expiration)\n"
"first.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"MX Localization (CFDI/EDI)\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Fiscal treatment (``account.journal.x_treatment``):\n"
"\n"
"============================= =========================== =============\n"
"Value                         Meaning                     CFDI Required\n"
"============================= =========================== =============\n"
"``fiscal_real``               Real fiscal operations      Yes\n"
"``fiscal_simulated``          Simulated fiscal (testing)  Yes\n"
"``not_fiscal_real``           Non-fiscal real             No\n"
"``not_fiscal_simulated``      Non-fiscal simulated        No\n"
"============================= =========================== =============\n"
"\n"
"Key overrides:\n"
"\n"
"- ``_compute_l10n_mx_edi_is_cfdi_needed``: checks ``x_treatment`` instead\n"
"  of blanket MX check\n"
"- ``create()``: strips taxes from non-fiscal moves\n"
"- ``_compute_show_send_button``: hides Send for non-fiscal\n"
"\n"
"PUE/PPD payment policy — default PUE; PPD if due date crosses month/year\n"
"boundary AND not ``cfdi_to_public`` AND not ``force_payment_policy_pue``.\n"
"\n"
"SAT status monitoring: ``l10n_mx_edi.document._fetch_and_update_sat_status``\n"
"processes documents in batches ordered by ``last_sat_state_sync_date``,\n"
"commits per-document, propagates network errors for retry. Transitions\n"
"from ``valid`` to ``cancelled`` post a message to the Discuss channel\n"
"``sat_status_cancellation_channel``. ``EstadoCancelacion`` parsing:\n"
"``Estado=Vigente`` with non-empty ``EstadoCancelacion`` is treated as\n"
"pending-cancellation.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Security Model\n"
"==============\n"
"\n"
"Custom privilege categories:\n"
"\n"
"=============== ==================================================== ==========\n"
"Category        Privileges                                           Count\n"
"=============== ==================================================== ==========\n"
"Accounting      Vendor/Customer Docs, Journal Entry (3-tier), Bank   6\n"
"                Statements, Cash Discount, Credit Limit\n"
"Master Data     Product Cost (readonly/manager)                      1\n"
"Vendors         Xiuman, Potatoes, General, Core Business             4\n"
"Supply Chain    Inventory Adj, Reconditioning, Printing (user/mgr),  4\n"
"                PO Lock\n"
"Sales           Liquidity Transfer, SO Lock                          2\n"
"Services        Project KPIs                                         1\n"
"Assets          Fleet, Equipment, Property, Machinery, Tools, IT     6\n"
"=============== ==================================================== ==========\n"
"\n"
"Hierarchical groups (``<`` means \"implies\"):\n"
"\n"
"- **Journal Entry:** ``group_account_move_draft`` < ``group_account_move_cancel`` < ``group_account_move_force_removal``\n"
"- **Product Cost:** ``group_product_cost_readonly`` < ``group_product_cost_manager``\n"
"- **Stock Printing:** ``group_stock_print_user`` < ``group_stock_print_manager``\n"
"- **POS:** ``group_pos_user`` < ``group_pos_officer`` < ``group_pos_manager``\n"
"\n"
"Granular stock permissions — ``stock.picking.type`` has 8 Many2many\n"
"fields linking users to actions (``can_todo_user_ids``,\n"
"``can_validate_user_ids``, ``can_check_availability_user_ids``,\n"
"``can_unreserve_user_ids``, ``can_scrap_user_ids``,\n"
"``can_return_user_ids``, ``can_open_detailed_operations_user_ids``,\n"
"``user_can_access_ids``). Empty list = no restriction.\n"
"``stock.group_stock_manager`` bypasses all granular checks.\n"
"\n"
"Record rules — only 4 defined in marin:\n"
"``sales_master_report_rule_manager/salesperson``,\n"
"``approval_request_sale_readonly_rule``,\n"
"``sales_master_report_sale_readonly_rule``.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Naming Patterns\n"
"===============\n"
"\n"
"=================================== ======================================== ================================\n"
"Pattern                             Example                                  Rule\n"
"=================================== ======================================== ================================\n"
"Security group XML ID               ``group_account_debt_manager``           ``group_{area}_{role}``\n"
"Privilege XML ID                    ``privilege_credit_limit``               ``privilege_{feature}``\n"
"User permission M2M                 ``can_validate_user_ids``                ``can_{action}_user_ids`` on\n"
"                                                                             ``stock.picking.type``\n"
"Show boolean                        ``show_validate``                        ``show_{action}`` on\n"
"                                                                             ``stock.picking``\n"
"User group boolean                  ``user_sale_manager``                    ``user_{group_name}`` computed\n"
"Score field                         ``score_hectares``                       ``score_{dimension}``\n"
"Force flag                          ``force_fully_invoiced``                 ``force_{state_name}``\n"
"Fiscal treatment                    ``x_treatment``                          ``x_`` prefix for non-standard\n"
"                                                                             accounting fields\n"
"Approval category ref               ``approval_category_1001``               ``approval_category_{seq_id}``\n"
"Cron XML ID                         ``ir_cron_merge_inactive_customers``     ``ir_cron_{action}``\n"
"=================================== ======================================== ================================\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Config Parameters (ir.config_parameter)\n"
"=======================================\n"
"\n"
"============================================================= ========= ========================================\n"
"Key                                                           Default   Used By\n"
"============================================================= ========= ========================================\n"
"``warehouse.theoretical_seconds_per_unit``                    60.0      Productivity metrics\n"
"``warehouse.productivity_buffer_time``                        30.0      Theoretical time calc\n"
"``warehouse.productivity_travel_speed``                       1.4       Distance/time (m/s)\n"
"``warehouse.productivity_checkin_location_id``                -         Default check-in location\n"
"``warehouse.productivity_default_location_dest_id``           -         Default destination (V5 calc)\n"
"``warehouse.default_ascent_time_per_level``                   5.0       V2 time window\n"
"``warehouse.default_descent_time_per_level``                  3.0       V4 time window\n"
"``warehouse_productivity.picking_seconds_per_unit``           30.0      V3 time window\n"
"``customer_merge_active``                                     False     Enable customer merge cron\n"
"``customer_merge_general_partner_id``                         0         Merge target partner\n"
"``customer_merge_min_orders``                                 2         Min orders to avoid merge\n"
"``customer_merge_interval_number`` / ``_interval_type``       3/months  Evaluation period\n"
"``document_l10n_mx_edi.sat_batch_size``                       100       SAT status check batch size\n"
"``document_l10n_mx_edi.sat_status_max_days``                  60        Max age for SAT status checks\n"
"============================================================= ========= ========================================\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Common Gotchas\n"
"==============\n"
"\n"
"1. **``stock.picking.read()`` auto-assigns user.** When productivity\n"
"   tracking is enabled and no user is set, ``read()`` assigns\n"
"   ``self.env.user`` to ``picking.user_id`` — reading modifies. Beware\n"
"   in batch operations and reports.\n"
"\n"
"2. **``sudo()`` sites** — customer merge cron, credit warning\n"
"   computation, sale order cancel (stock.move ACL), picking validate\n"
"   (sale access), GL dashboard data, SAT status fetch. Restricted\n"
"   contact editing moved to a whitelist mechanism\n"
"   (``partner_group_restricted``) — see that module's README.\n"
"\n"
"3. **Granular permissions are additive to manager.**\n"
"   ``stock.group_stock_manager`` bypasses ALL granular checks; the\n"
"   ``can_*_user_ids`` fields only gate non-manager users.\n"
"\n"
"5. **Custom removal default.** When no strategy is set on category or\n"
"   location, marin defaults to ``refurbished + fefo + priority``\n"
"   (not stock's default FIFO).\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_agro_base
msgid ""
"=========\n"
"Agro Base\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"Foundational agronomic master data for AgroMarin, plus the operational fact\n"
"table built on it. Owns the catalogs, the **Agronomy** application shell, and\n"
"since **19.0.3.0.0** ``agro.campaign`` and its EAV attribute profile -- the\n"
"former ``agro_surface`` module, absorbed whole.\n"
"\n"
"Identity, roles and interactions\n"
"================================\n"
"\n"
"Since **19.0.2.0.0** the catalogs are organised in three layers rather than as\n"
"a flat set. The five organism catalogs used to discriminate on what a thing\n"
"*does to a farm* while duplicating what the thing *is*, and the seeded data\n"
"contradicted itself as a result: nematodes were filed as a disease\n"
"(*Meloidogyne*), as a beneficial (*Steinernema*) and as a pest type; *Bacillus*\n"
"and *Trichoderma* were beneficials while the same kingdoms were disease types;\n"
"*Sorghum bicolor* was a crop and *S. halepense* a weed, the only difference\n"
"being whether anyone planted it.\n"
"\n"
"* **``agro.organism``** owns identity: the name, the binomial, a\n"
"  self-referential taxonomic tree (family → species → cultivar/breed), the\n"
"  ``lineage`` and ``cellularity``, and thermal time. ``lineage`` is\n"
"  deliberately not called *kingdom* -- the acellular agents have none, and\n"
"  oomycetes are not fungi, a distinction with teeth since FRAC 4 phenylamides\n"
"  control oomycetes and do nothing to true fungi. ``cellularity`` admits\n"
"  ``disputed`` as a real answer rather than forcing a side on whether a virus\n"
"  is an organism.\n"
"* **Roles** -- ``agro.crop``, ``agro.livestock``, ``agro.pest``, ``agro.weed``,\n"
"  ``agro.pathogen``, ``agro.beneficial``, ``agro.variety``, ``agro.breed`` --\n"
"  delegate to it through ``_inherits``. Each keeps its own primary key, so\n"
"  every foreign key from ``agro.campaign``, ``marin`` and the SIAP bridge\n"
"  survived the merge untouched. One organism may hold several roles at once,\n"
"  and retiring a role does not retire the taxon.\n"
"* **``agro.interaction``** replaces the ten relations that all encoded \"A\n"
"  affects B\" -- damages, infects, competes, transmits, preys_on, parasitizes,\n"
"  antagonizes, pollinates, resists. ``severity`` lives on the edge, where it\n"
"  was always true: a whitefly is critical on tomato, where it vectors TYLCV,\n"
"  and a nuisance on maize.\n"
"\n"
"Identity is the **binomial**, not the name. Vernacular names repeat freely --\n"
"the SIAP Nomcultivo registers \"Potato\" once per crop group with no binomial to\n"
"tell them apart -- while ``scientific_name`` is unique, and a role created\n"
"against an existing binomial attaches to that organism instead of minting a\n"
"second one.\n"
"\n"
"Provides\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"* **Plant catalogs**: ``agro.crop``, ``agro.variety`` (per-crop), ``agro.grade``\n"
"  (commercial caliber), ``agro.crop.family`` (botanical family with a\n"
"  monocot/dicot class, for rotation planning) and ``agro.crop.group`` (BI\n"
"  grouping; the Mexican agrochemical value master is added by\n"
"  ``agro_surface_l10n_mx``). Crops carry their botanical identity\n"
"  (``scientific_name``, ``family_id``) and growing cycle (``lifecycle``,\n"
"  ``cycle_days``); varieties may override ``cycle_days`` and declare the\n"
"  diseases/pests they resist through rated ``resists`` interactions\n"
"  (``resistance_ids``, reverse ``resisted_by_ids``): each pairing carries a\n"
"  ``resistance_level`` (immune / resistant / moderately resistant / tolerant /\n"
"  susceptible) rather than a bare boolean link. Since the edge joins two\n"
"  organisms rather than keying on a variety, resistance is recordable at any\n"
"  rank -- \"all our potatoes tolerate PVY\" was not expressible before.\n"
"  Calibers carry objective bounds (``caliber_min`` / ``caliber_max`` in a\n"
"  ``caliber_uom_id`` unit from the standard ``uom`` catalog).\n"
"  Crops also carry an **agronomic envelope** that drives planning and\n"
"  suitability: thermal time (``base_temp_c`` for growing degree-days,\n"
"  ``optimal_temp_min_c`` / ``optimal_temp_max_c``), preferred soil reaction\n"
"  (``ph_min`` / ``ph_max``, mirroring ``agro.soil.type`` so crop↔soil\n"
"  suitability is computable) and ``salinity_tolerance``, planting geometry\n"
"  (``row_spacing_cm`` / ``plant_spacing_cm``, with the derived\n"
"  ``plant_density`` in plants/ha) and irrigation planning (``rooting_depth_cm``,\n"
"  ``water_requirement_mm`` -- the seasonal ETc integral -- with the FAO-56 stage\n"
"  crop coefficients ``kc_ini`` / ``kc_mid`` / ``kc_end``, the growth-stage\n"
"  lengths ``stage_days_ini`` / ``dev`` / ``mid`` / ``late`` (summed in\n"
"  ``stage_days_total``) and the depletion fraction ``depletion_fraction_p``, so\n"
"  daily crop water (hydric) demand ``ETc = Kc × ETo`` can be integrated stage by\n"
"  stage and the RAW = p × TAW irrigation trigger derived against the rooting\n"
"  depth). Thermal time is closed out with an ``upper_temp_c``\n"
"  cutoff (the daily mean is capped there before GDD accrual) and a\n"
"  ``gdd_to_maturity`` target, so heat-unit accumulation -- not just the calendar\n"
"  ``cycle_days`` -- can predict maturity across seasons. A nutrient budget pairs\n"
"  a reference ``typical_yield_t_ha`` with elemental removal coefficients for the\n"
"  primary macronutrients ``n_removal_kg_t`` / ``p_removal_kg_t`` /\n"
"  ``k_removal_kg_t`` and the secondary nutrients ``s_removal_kg_t`` /\n"
"  ``ca_removal_kg_t`` / ``mg_removal_kg_t`` (same elemental basis as the\n"
"  fertilizer ``p_elem_pct`` / ``k_elem_pct`` and its guaranteed ``s_pct`` /\n"
"  ``ca_pct`` / ``mg_pct``; sulfur matters for the Allium and Brassica crops) and\n"
"  derives the per-hectare removal ``*_removal_kg_ha`` (yield × per-tonne\n"
"  removal), the crop-demand side of a fertilizer-rate calculation across any of\n"
"  the six nutrients. Families add the rotation-planning traits\n"
"  ``nitrogen_fixing`` (seeded on Fabaceae) and ``rotation_return_years``.\n"
"* **Livestock catalogs**: ``agro.livestock`` (species) and ``agro.breed``\n"
"  (per-species), parallel to crop → variety.\n"
"* **Health catalogs**: ``agro.pathogen`` (the causal organism),\n"
"  ``agro.disease`` (the pathology it produces, or a physiological disorder when\n"
"  it has none) and ``agro.pest``. Hosts are ``infects`` / ``damages``\n"
"  interactions carrying their own ``severity``, reachable from either end\n"
"  (``host_interaction_ids`` on the aggressor, ``pest_interaction_ids`` /\n"
"  ``pathogen_interaction_ids`` on the host); a disorder keeps a direct\n"
"  Many2many, having no organism to be the other end of an edge. Splitting the\n"
"  pathogen from the pathology is what gives viruses a row at all -- nine of\n"
"  them previously existed only as text in a ``scientific_name`` Char, so\n"
"  nothing could point at one. Conditions add a numeric infection\n"
"  window (``infection_temp_min_c`` / ``opt`` / ``max``, ``min_leaf_wetness_h``,\n"
"  ``min_humidity_pct`` and a ``forecast_model`` reference) alongside the\n"
"  narrative ``favorable_conditions``; ``is_infection_favorable()`` scores\n"
"  observed weather against it and a stored ``forecast_ready`` flag marks the\n"
"  conditions carrying enough data to alert on. A vector transmits the\n"
"  *pathogen* (``vector_interaction_ids``, reverse\n"
"  ``vectored_interaction_ids``); pests add an\n"
"  ``economic_threshold`` (IPM action threshold) -- a free-text narrative plus a\n"
"  machine-evaluable ``economic_threshold_value`` / ``economic_threshold_unit``\n"
"  pair that ``exceeds_threshold(count)`` scores a scouting count against, the\n"
"  pest-side counterpart to the disease infection window. For resistance\n"
"  management each\n"
"  control product carries its mode-of-action group(s)\n"
"  (``product.template.moa_group_ids`` → ``agro.moa.group``, the FRAC / IRAC /\n"
"  HRAC target-site classification); diseases, pests and weeds roll up the\n"
"  distinct groups their products span (``control_moa_group_ids``) with a\n"
"  ``moa_diversity`` count -- the palette available to rotate. Each control\n"
"  ``product.template`` also carries the structured label restrictions that gate\n"
"  a spray decision -- ``phi_days`` (pre-harvest interval), ``rei_hours``\n"
"  (worker re-entry interval) and ``max_applications_per_cycle`` (the label /\n"
"  RAC cap that bounds how far one mode of action can be leaned on) -- the\n"
"  machine-usable counterpart to the free-text label held in\n"
"  ``product_agronomic_docs``.\n"
"* **Beneficial organisms**: ``agro.beneficial`` -- the natural-enemy side of\n"
"  IPM, catalogued so a biological option can be weighed alongside the chemical\n"
"  one. Each is classified by ``beneficial_type`` (predator, parasitoid,\n"
"  entomopathogen, microbial antagonist, pollinator), flagged\n"
"  ``commercially_available`` for augmentative release, and linked to the pests\n"
"  it suppresses and/or the pathogens it antagonizes\n"
"  (``target_interaction_ids``, typed ``preys_on`` / ``parasitizes`` /\n"
"  ``antagonizes`` by the service it provides) plus the biocontrol\n"
"  ``product.template`` records that supply it. Pests and pathogens expose the\n"
"  reverse ``enemy_interaction_ids``, so a control page can surface the living\n"
"  controls next to the sprays. Seeded with common agents (Trichogramma,\n"
"  Encarsia, lady beetle, Bacillus thuringiensis, Beauveria, Trichoderma, ...).\n"
"* **Weeds & disorders**: ``agro.weed`` (competing plants classified by\n"
"  ``weed_type`` / ``life_cycle`` and linked to control herbicides) is a role on\n"
"  the organism, so a weed and a crop can be the same plant. A physiological\n"
"  disorder is no longer a catalog of its own: it is an ``agro.disease`` with no\n"
"  ``pathogen_id``, classified by ``abiotic_type``. That model argued for its own\n"
"  existence on the grounds that \"a disorder has no causal organism\", which --\n"
"  once the organism is a nullable foreign key -- is a value rather than a\n"
"  reason for a second table. Crops\n"
"  expose ``weed_interaction_ids`` and the direct ``disorder_ids``; livestock\n"
"  exposes ``disorder_ids``.\n"
"* **Fertilizers**: ``agro.fertilizer`` -- mineral/organic/biofertilizer inputs\n"
"  with a full guaranteed analysis (N-P₂O₅-K₂O, secondary Ca/Mg/S,\n"
"  micronutrients B/Zn/Fe/Mn/Cu/Mo, organic matter), a nitrogen speciation split\n"
"  (``n_no3_pct`` / ``n_nh4_pct`` / ``n_urea_pct``, bounded to the total N) and\n"
"  ``cl_pct`` chloride for chloride-sensitive crops, solution/fertigation\n"
"  properties (``ph``, ``ec``, liquid ``density_kg_l`` and the ``salt_index``\n"
"  for banding safety), tank-mix ``incompatible_fertilizer_ids``, supplying\n"
"  ``product.template`` records and recommended crops (reverse\n"
"  ``agro.crop.fertilizer_ids``). The ``npk_label`` compute renders the classic\n"
"  grade (e.g. 18-46-0), and ``p_elem_pct`` / ``k_elem_pct`` expose the\n"
"  elemental P and K equivalents (P₂O₅ × 0.4364, K₂O × 0.8301) used in\n"
"  nutrient-budget math. Tank-mix ``incompatible_fertilizer_ids`` is kept\n"
"  symmetric automatically -- flagging A incompatible with B also flags B with\n"
"  A. Guaranteed-analysis figures are bounded to 0-100 % individually and the\n"
"  mineral fractions cannot sum past 100 %.\n"
"* **Soil types**: ``agro.soil.type`` -- classifies a soil along three axes\n"
"  (USDA ``texture`` class, USDA Soil Taxonomy ``taxonomy_order``, WRB\n"
"  ``soil_group``) and records the agronomic properties that drive crop\n"
"  suitability (particle-size composition, ``drainage``,\n"
"  ``water_holding_capacity``, ``fertility``, pH range, organic matter,\n"
"  cation-exchange capacity ``cec`` and salinity ``salinity_ece`` with a derived\n"
"  USDA ``salinity_class``). The\n"
"  sand/silt/clay fractions must add up to 100 % (or all be blank) since a\n"
"  soil's texture is its point on the USDA triangle, and pH is bounded to the\n"
"  0-14 scale. Seeded\n"
"  with the 12 taxonomy orders and the 12 texture classes. Crop↔soil suitability\n"
"  is the rated ``agro.crop.soil.suitability`` through-model\n"
"  (``agro.crop.soil_suitability_ids`` / ``agro.soil.type.crop_suitability_ids``),\n"
"  each pairing carrying an FAO land-suitability ``rating`` (S1 highly suitable …\n"
"  N not suitable) instead of a bare link. A computed ``suggested_rating``\n"
"  advises that class from the crop's preferred pH range and salinity tolerance\n"
"  against the soil's pH and ``salinity_ece`` (the limiting factor wins, per\n"
"  Liebig); the manual ``rating`` stays authoritative and can override it.\n"
"* **Application shell & security**: the *Agronomy* root menu, the\n"
"  ``Configuration`` / ``Reporting`` / ``Business Intelligence`` sub-menus, the\n"
"  *Agronomy* privilege and the ``group_agro_user`` (read catalogs) /\n"
"  ``group_agro_manager`` (maintain catalogs) groups.\n"
"\n"
"Decision-support engines\n"
"========================\n"
"\n"
"The agronomic envelope is not just stored, it is *computed against*. The\n"
"catalog models expose reusable methods (parallel to ``agro.disease``'s\n"
"``is_infection_favorable``) that turn the master data into the day-to-day\n"
"numbers, so operational modules consume calculations rather than re-derive\n"
"them:\n"
"\n"
"* **Thermal time** (``agro.crop``): ``gdd_for_day(mean_temp_c)`` accrues\n"
"  growing degree-days by the horizontal-cutoff method (mean capped at\n"
"  ``upper_temp_c``, base ``base_temp_c`` subtracted, floored at zero);\n"
"  ``accumulate_gdd(daily_means)`` sums a season and ``gdd_progress(gdd)``\n"
"  reports the fraction of the way to ``gdd_to_maturity`` -- weather-robust\n"
"  maturity tracking that holds where calendar days drift.\n"
"* **Crop water demand** (``agro.crop``): ``kc_for_day(day)`` reconstructs the\n"
"  four-stage FAO-56 Kc curve from the stage lengths and coefficients, and\n"
"  ``etc_for_series(eto_series, start_day=1)`` integrates ``ETc = Kc × ETo``\n"
"  day by day, so seasonal water use follows real (or forecast) ETo instead of\n"
"  the lumped ``water_requirement_mm``.\n"
"* **Irrigation trigger** (``agro.crop`` × ``agro.soil.type``): the soil's\n"
"  ``total_available_water(rooting_depth_cm)`` gives TAW from its available\n"
"  water capacity (measured ``awc_mm_m``, else a USDA texture-class or\n"
"  water-holding-capacity fallback), and the crop's\n"
"  ``readily_available_water(soil)`` returns ``RAW = p × TAW`` -- the depletion\n"
"  depth at which irrigation should refill the root zone.\n"
"* **Fertilizer rate** (``agro.crop`` × ``agro.fertilizer``):\n"
"  ``fertilizer_rate(fertilizer, nutrient, use_efficiency, soil_supply)`` closes\n"
"  the nutrient budget -- ``(removal − soil_supply) / (elemental_fraction ×\n"
"  use_efficiency)`` -- returning the kg/ha of product needed to meet a\n"
"  nutrient's removal on an elemental basis, for any of the six budgeted\n"
"  nutrients (N, P, K, S, Ca, Mg); ``nutrient_removal()`` exposes the demand side\n"
"  alone.\n"
"* **Salinity yield loss** (``agro.crop``):\n"
"  ``salinity_yield_loss_pct(ece)`` applies the Maas-Hoffman threshold-slope\n"
"  model -- no loss up to ``salinity_threshold_ece``, then a linear decline at\n"
"  ``salinity_slope_pct`` per dS/m, capped at 100 % -- using the crop's numeric\n"
"  response when set and representative per-tolerance-group parameters\n"
"  otherwise. It is what the crop↔soil ``suggested_rating`` maps onto the FAO\n"
"  suitability classes, replacing the earlier threshold-multiple heuristic.\n"
"\n"
"Agricultural campaigns (19.0.3.0.0)\n"
"====================================\n"
"\n"
"``agro.campaign`` is one record per **agricultural campaign**: a customer's\n"
"planting season for one crop in one area. Its identity -- and its uniqueness\n"
"rule -- is *partner x season x crop x variety x city x company*; ``hectares`` is\n"
"one measurement it carries, not what it is. One physical farm yields N campaigns\n"
"over time, one per season and crop.\n"
"\n"
"It was called ``agro.surface``, in its own module, until 19.0.3.0.0. That name\n"
"was wrong in a way that misled rather than merely read badly: the record was\n"
"never a piece of land, and both the docstring and the uniqueness key already\n"
"said so. The module was folded into ``agro_base``, which already owned every\n"
"catalog it consumed.\n"
"\n"
"* **The EAV profile keeps its model names.** ``agro.attribute``,\n"
"  ``agro.attribute.value`` and ``agro.campaign.attribute.line`` are\n"
"  unchanged, deliberately -- renaming the fact table is one table to migrate,\n"
"  renaming the family would have been four. The line's foreign key does follow\n"
"  the model it points at (``surface_id`` -> ``campaign_id``), as do\n"
"  ``res.partner.surface_ids`` -> ``campaign_ids`` and the m2m table\n"
"  ``agro_surface_grade_rel`` -> ``agro_campaign_grade_rel``.\n"
"* Production-size classification no longer lives on the campaign. The\n"
"  ``production_size`` numeric_range attribute is still shipped and still\n"
"  half-open (``[min, max)``, the top bucket open-ended), but the classifying\n"
"  call site is ``agro_partner_scoring``, which scores the partner rather than\n"
"  the campaign.\n"
"* ``soil_type_id`` is the seam into this module's agronomy engines: with a soil\n"
"  chosen, ``soil_suitability`` and ``readily_available_water_mm`` become\n"
"  computable for that particular cultivation.\n"
"\n"
"Migration\n"
"---------\n"
"\n"
"``absorb_surface.py`` performs the absorption, from **both** routes, because a\n"
"database that predates ``agro_base`` *installs* it and migration scripts do not\n"
"run on install:\n"
"\n"
"* ``pre_init_hook`` -- the production route. The live database has no\n"
"  ``agro_base`` row at all.\n"
"* ``migrations/19.0.3.0.0/pre-migrate.py`` -- a deployment already carrying\n"
"  ``agro_base``.\n"
"\n"
"It renames the table, sequence, columns, constraints and indexes; rewrites\n"
"``ir_model``, ``ir_model_fields``, ``ir_model_data``, ``ir_act_window``,\n"
"``ir_ui_view``, ``ir_filters``, ``ir_model_constraint`` and\n"
"``ir_model_relation``; and retires the ``agro_surface`` module row. It must run\n"
"before this module's data files load, or the end-of-load orphan sweep deletes\n"
"each view and menu and the reload re-creates it with a **new database id**,\n"
"breaking every action, inheriting view and Studio customisation holding the old\n"
"one.\n"
"\n"
"Two of ``agro_surface``'s own migrations are replayed here because most\n"
"databases never reached them and they die with the module: the hand-made name\n"
"indexes handed to ``models.UniqueIndex`` (its 19.0.1.6.0), and the conversion of\n"
"numeric bands from inclusive to half-open bounds plus the re-classification of\n"
"every campaign's stored bucket (its 19.0.1.5.0).\n"
"\n"
"Backward compatibility\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"* The moved records keep their identifiers; ``agro_base``'s ``pre_init_hook``\n"
"  re-tags the existing ``ir_model_data`` rows from ``agro_surface`` to\n"
"  ``agro_base``, so campaigns, products and saved data keep pointing at the same\n"
"  crop/variety/grade rows (no duplicates).\n"
"* The ``agro_surface.group_agro_user`` / ``agro_surface.group_agro_manager``\n"
"  aliases are **gone** as of 19.0.3.0.0, with the module that published them.\n"
"  Every reference now names ``agro_base.`` directly. A view gated on an\n"
"  unresolvable group is stripped silently for everyone, so\n"
"  ``tests/test_agro_security.py`` guards that no arch names a group the\n"
"  resolver cannot find.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_ai_project
msgid ""
"==========\n"
"AI Project\n"
"==========\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Beta-yellow.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Beta\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-LGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: LGPL-3\n"
".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-AgroMarin%2Fagromarin--addons-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin-addons/tree/19.0/ai_project\n"
"    :alt: AgroMarin/agromarin-addons\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3|\n"
"\n"
"AI-powered task creation and automatic code generation for Odoo 19.0.\n"
"\n"
"This module integrates AI capabilities into the project management workflow,\n"
"enabling automatic requirement gathering, technical analysis, and code generation\n"
"through natural conversation with AI assistants.\n"
"\n"
"**Key Features:**\n"
"\n"
"- **Requirement Gathering**: Capture requirements using COAST framework through AI conversation\n"
"- **Technical Analysis**: Analyze requirements with codebase context and generate technical subtasks\n"
"- **Code Generation**: Automatically generate Odoo modules following coding standards\n"
"- **Git Integration**: Create branches, commits, and Pull Requests automatically\n"
"- **GitHub PR Sync**: Track Pull Request status directly in tasks\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Installation\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"This module requires the following dependencies:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Odoo Modules:**\n"
"\n"
"   - ``ai_app`` - Base AI application\n"
"   - ``gateway_ml`` - Vendor clients, including the Claude SDK subprocess client\n"
"   - ``api_ai_agent`` - Registers Claude as a provider ``ai.agent`` can select\n"
"   - ``project`` - Project management\n"
"   - ``mixin_encryption`` - Field-level encryption for stored tokens\n"
"   - ``api_github`` - GitHub REST client for the pull-request flow\n"
"\n"
"2. **Python Packages:**\n"
"\n"
"   .. code-block:: bash\n"
"\n"
"      pip install requests\n"
"\n"
"3. **External Tools (for code generation):**\n"
"\n"
"   - GitHub CLI (``gh``) authenticated\n"
"   - Git configured with user name and email\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"API Keys\n"
"--------\n"
"\n"
"The module uses AI agents configured in Odoo. Ensure the following agents are properly\n"
"configured with API keys:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Requirements Assistant** - For COAST framework gathering\n"
"2. **Technical Analysis Agent** - For technical planning\n"
"3. **Code Generation Agent** - For automatic code generation\n"
"\n"
"Project Setup\n"
"-------------\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to **Project** app\n"
"2. Open project configuration\n"
"3. Enable **AI Support** checkbox\n"
"4. Tasks created in this project will have AI workflow enabled\n"
"\n"
"GitHub Integration\n"
"------------------\n"
"\n"
"For users who need to sync GitHub PR status:\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to **Settings** > **Users** > Select user\n"
"2. In **Security** tab, configure **GitHub Token**\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"AI Support Workflow\n"
"-------------------\n"
"\n"
"Tasks with AI Support follow this workflow:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Analysis Pending** - Ready for technical context specification\n"
"2. **Analysis In Progress** - AI analyzing requirements\n"
"3. **Analysis Done** - Technical subtasks generated\n"
"4. **Code Pending** - Code generation in progress\n"
"5. **Code Generated** - Pull Request created\n"
"6. **Testing** - Deployed to test environment\n"
"7. **Approved** - Testing passed\n"
"8. **Scheduled** - Ready for production\n"
"9. **Production** - Deployed\n"
"10. **Done** - Completed\n"
"\n"
"Creating Tasks from AI Conversation\n"
"-----------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"The module provides AI tools for creating tasks through conversation:\n"
"\n"
"1. User describes their requirement in natural language\n"
"2. AI gathers Context, Objective, and Scenario (COAST framework)\n"
"3. Task is automatically created with structured requirements\n"
"4. Technical analysis can be triggered to generate subtasks\n"
"\n"
"Technical Analysis\n"
"------------------\n"
"\n"
"After capturing requirements:\n"
"\n"
"1. Click **Add Technical Specs** to specify modules and models\n"
"2. Add architecture notes and constraints\n"
"3. Click **Request Analysis** to trigger AI analysis\n"
"4. AI generates technical subtasks with:\n"
"\n"
"   - Detailed requirements\n"
"   - Acceptance criteria\n"
"   - Improvement opportunities\n"
"\n"
"Automatic Code Generation\n"
"-------------------------\n"
"\n"
"When technical analysis is complete:\n"
"\n"
"1. Click **Request Code**\n"
"2. System runs in background (3-5 minutes)\n"
"3. AI generates complete Odoo module:\n"
"\n"
"   - Models with proper structure\n"
"   - Views (form, list, search)\n"
"   - Security (access rights, groups)\n"
"   - Data files\n"
"\n"
"4. Creates Git branch, commit, and Pull Request\n"
"5. Task updated with PR URL\n"
"\n"
"GitHub PR Synchronization\n"
"-------------------------\n"
"\n"
"To sync PR status from GitHub:\n"
"\n"
"1. Ensure task has **PR URL** field populated\n"
"2. Click **Sync GitHub PR**\n"
"3. Task description updates with:\n"
"\n"
"   - PR status (open/merged/closed)\n"
"   - File changes\n"
"   - Preview environment URL (if available)\n"
"   - Approval status\n"
"\n"
"Known Issues / Roadmap\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"- Improve code validation before commit\n"
"- Add support for multi-module generation\n"
"- Implement deployment automation\n"
"- Enhanced error recovery for API failures\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin-addons/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin-addons/issues/new?body=module:%20ai_project%0Aversion:%2019.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"- `AgroMarin <https://www.agromarin.com>`__:\n"
"\n"
"  - Jose Suniaga\n"
"\n"
"Maintainers\n"
"-----------\n"
"\n"
"This module is maintained by AgroMarin.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://www.agromarin.com/web/image/res.company/1/logo\n"
"   :alt: AgroMarin\n"
"   :target: https://www.agromarin.com\n"
"\n"
"AgroMarin is a company specialized in agricultural ERP solutions\n"
"based on Odoo.\n"
"\n"
"This module is part of the `AgroMarin/agromarin-addons <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin-addons/tree/19.0/ai_project>`_ project on GitHub.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_marin_rma
msgid ""
"==========\n"
"Marin RMA\n"
"==========\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Production-green.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Production/Stable\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-LGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: LGPL-3\n"
".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-Agro--Marin%2Fagromarin-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin/tree/19.0/marin_rma\n"
"    :alt: Agro-Marin/agromarin\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3|\n"
"\n"
"This module provides a comprehensive RMA (Return Merchandise Authorization) system for managing\n"
"customer claims and complaints with full traceability integration.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Overview\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"The Marin RMA module allows you to manage customer claims with complete traceability from\n"
"the claim to the production process. It integrates seamlessly with sales, inventory, and\n"
"manufacturing modules to provide a complete claim management solution.\n"
"\n"
"Features\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"* **Complete Claim Management**\n"
"\n"
"  * Create and manage customer claims with detailed information\n"
"  * 7-state workflow (draft → sent → approved → in_progress → to_close → done/cancel)\n"
"  * Assign responsible parties and categorize claims by reason\n"
"\n"
"* **Sales Integration**\n"
"\n"
"  * Create RMA claims directly from sale orders\n"
"  * Guided wizard for bulk RMA creation\n"
"  * Automatic filtering of delivered and invoiced products\n"
"  * Quantity validation against delivered/invoiced amounts\n"
"\n"
"* **Manufacturing Integration**\n"
"\n"
"  * Link claims to production orders via lot/serial numbers\n"
"  * View related RMAs from manufacturing orders via smart button\n"
"  * Auto-detection of production orders based on lot numbers\n"
"\n"
"* **Traceability**\n"
"\n"
"  * Complete traceability from claim to production process\n"
"  * Track claims by product, lot/serial number, and batch\n"
"  * Link to specific sale orders and deliveries\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"To configure this module:\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to **Sales → Configuration → RMA Reasons**\n"
"2. Create claim reason categories for classification\n"
"3. Configure user permissions:\n"
"\n"
"   * **RMA User**: Basic access to create and manage own RMAs\n"
"   * **RMA Manager**: Full access to all RMAs and approval workflow\n"
"   * **Manufacturing RMA User**: Read-only access to production-related RMAs\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Creating RMA from Sale Order\n"
"-----------------------------\n"
"\n"
"1. Navigate to **Sales → Orders → Sales Orders**\n"
"2. Open a confirmed and invoiced sale order\n"
"3. Click on **Create Claim** button\n"
"4. Select products and quantities to claim\n"
"5. Add claim reasons and descriptions\n"
"6. Confirm to create individual RMA orders\n"
"\n"
"Managing RMA Orders\n"
"-------------------\n"
"\n"
"1. Go to **Sales → After-Sales → RMA Orders**\n"
"2. Create or open an RMA order\n"
"3. Follow the workflow:\n"
"\n"
"   * **Draft**: Initial state, edit all information\n"
"   * **Approval Request**: Send for manager approval\n"
"   * **Approved**: Claim approved, ready to process\n"
"   * **In Progress**: Claim being processed\n"
"   * **To Close**: Ready for closure\n"
"   * **Closed**: Claim resolved and closed\n"
"   * **Cancelled**: Claim cancelled\n"
"\n"
"Viewing RMAs from Manufacturing\n"
"-------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"1. Open a **Manufacturing Order**\n"
"2. Click on the **RMAs** smart button\n"
"3. View all related claims for the production order\n"
"\n"
"Known Issues / Roadmap\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"* Integration with credit notes and refund processes\n"
"* Automated email notifications for state changes\n"
"* Dashboard and reporting for claim analytics\n"
"* Integration with quality control module\n"
"* Mobile app support for field claim creation\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin/issues/new?body=module:%20marin_rma%0Aversion:%2019.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* Agro-Marin\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"* Agro-Marin Development Team\n"
"* Migrated to Odoo 19.0 by lumpuy\n"
"\n"
"Maintainers\n"
"-----------\n"
"\n"
"This module is maintained by Agro-Marin.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://www.agromarin.mx/logo.png\n"
"   :alt: Agro-Marin\n"
"   :target: https://www.agromarin.mx\n"
"\n"
"Agro-Marin is a company specializing in agricultural and marine solutions,\n"
"committed to providing high-quality ERP solutions for the agricultural sector.\n"
"\n"
"To contribute to this module, please visit https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_syngenta_edi
msgid ""
"============\n"
"Syngenta EDI\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"Sends AgroMarin's sell-out and inventory reports to Syngenta's web service.\n"
"\n"
"Syngenta, as a manufacturer, wants to know what its distributor sold and what\n"
"it still holds. This module builds those two reports and hands them to\n"
"``exchange``, which owns the conversation with the counterparty: who to call,\n"
"whether it arrived, what the answer was, and when to ask again.\n"
"\n"
"The two documents\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"+----------------------------+------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
"| Model                      | Syngenta path    | What it reports                                             |\n"
"+============================+==================+=============================================================+\n"
"| ``syngenta.sale.report``   | ``Sellout``      | What a customer consumed under a commercial agreement       |\n"
"+----------------------------+------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
"| ``syngenta.stock.report``  | ``inventario``   | What the distributor still holds, per product               |\n"
"+----------------------------+------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
"\n"
"Both post a JSON envelope of ``clave_Distribuidor``, the distributor's name and\n"
"a ``productLines`` array. **The envelope names the distributor differently per\n"
"document** -- ``nombre_distribuidor`` for Sellout, ``nombre_Distribuidor`` for\n"
"inventario -- and that is deliberate, not a typo: both have been accepted since\n"
"this module's first commit. The names live in ``DISTRIBUTOR_KEY`` in\n"
"``models/mixin_syngenta_edi.py`` so the two builders cannot drift apart.\n"
"\n"
"``tests/sell_out.json`` is the only field-level artefact we hold from Syngenta.\n"
"It is a 2020 sample, it is not loaded by anything, and it disagrees with the\n"
"live payload in two places (``rFC`` where we send ``rfc``, and two keys it does\n"
"not carry). We follow the wire rather than the sample; settling it needs\n"
"Syngenta's current field spec.\n"
"\n"
"How a report is sent\n"
"====================\n"
"\n"
"1. ``action_send`` on the report adds an ``exchange.transmission`` with intent\n"
"   ``issue`` and asks it to send. A report whose transmission is still in\n"
"   flight is refused rather than sent twice.\n"
"2. ``exchange.protocol.syngenta._check_message`` refuses the document if the\n"
"   company has no ``syngenta_customer_code`` or the report has no lines.\n"
"   Nothing reaches the network in that case; the transmission settles rejected\n"
"   with the reason.\n"
"3. ``_send_message`` posts the JSON. The endpoint record\n"
"   (``data/api_service_data.xml``) owns the URL, the timeout pair and the retry\n"
"   policy -- this module passes none of them.\n"
"4. ``_read_body`` reads Syngenta's verdict into a ``Verdict``. An answer that is\n"
"   not recognisably Syngenta's is retried rather than believed: an empty body\n"
"   is not an acceptance. The report's ``state`` is derived from the verdict,\n"
"   never set by hand.\n"
"\n"
"Two things worth knowing\n"
"========================\n"
"\n"
"**The inventory report is a snapshot.** ``syngenta.stock.report.line`` rows with\n"
"no ``report_id`` are the editable catalogue; sending a report freezes a copy of\n"
"that catalogue onto it. Editing the catalogue afterwards does not change what an\n"
"already-sent report says it reported.\n"
"\n"
"**A report Syngenta has ruled on is closed.** Its header fields and its lines\n"
"refuse create, write and unlink once the report is ``sent``, ``done`` or\n"
"``error``, and cancelling a report whose transmission is still in flight is\n"
"refused outright -- Syngenta publishes no annulment endpoint, so a document they\n"
"already hold cannot be withdrawn from here.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"+---------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
"| Where                                       | What                                                                          |\n"
"+=============================================+===============================================================================+\n"
"| Users                                       | Assign the **Syngenta EDI** group; the app's menu is gated on it.             |\n"
"+---------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
"| Company form                                | ``syngenta_customer_code`` -- the distributor id Syngenta knows us by.        |\n"
"|                                             | Required to send.                                                             |\n"
"+---------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
"| ``integration.service`` ``syngenta``        | URL, ``environment`` (test or production), timeouts, retry and rate limits.   |\n"
"+---------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
"| Product                                     | ``manufacturer_id`` must be the Syngenta partner; ``manufacturer_pref`` is    |\n"
"|                                             | the code sent as ``codeProduct_Distribuidor``.                                |\n"
"+---------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_telegram_bot
msgid ""
"============\n"
"Telegram Bot\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"This module provides the core infrastructure for integrating Telegram bots with Odoo.\n"
"\n"
"Features\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"* Telegram Bot API wrapper (``sendMessage``, ``sendDocument``, ``getFile``,\n"
"  ``answerCallbackQuery``, ``editMessageReplyMarkup``) on top of ``integration``\n"
"* Webhook handler at ``/telegram/webhook/<bot_token>`` with\n"
"  ``X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token`` verification\n"
"* **Exactly-once update handling**: Telegram redeliveries are rejected by\n"
"  ``telegram.update``, and a handler re-run by Odoo's ``retrying()`` replays the\n"
"  API answers it already got instead of sending them twice\n"
"* Command routing with three-tier permission model (unlinked, partner,\n"
"  internal user), where \"internal\" excludes portal and other share users\n"
"* Base commands: ``/start``, ``/ayuda``, ``/quiensoy``\n"
"* Chat session state machine with per-chat rate limiting (token bucket via\n"
"  ``credential``) and context storage for multi-step flows\n"
"* Markdown helpers that escape interpolated values, so a partner name carrying\n"
"  ``_``, ``*``, ``` ` ``` or ``[`` cannot make Telegram reject the message\n"
"* Automatic partner linking by Telegram username, case- and ``@``-insensitive\n"
"* Inbound/outbound message history with per-chat ``msg_uid`` deduplication,\n"
"  15-day auto-vacuum for delivered traffic and 90-day for failures\n"
"* Inline keyboard support (buttons with ``callback_data``)\n"
"* Log filter that masks bot tokens in werkzeug output\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"1. Create (or reuse) a ``credential.credential`` record with service\n"
"   ``telegram`` and the bot token in ``bearer_token``.\n"
"2. Go to Telegram > Telegram Bots and create a bot referencing that\n"
"   credential.\n"
"3. **Press Register Webhook on the bot form.** It generates a random 32-byte\n"
"   secret, stores it as the webhook receiver's credential and registers\n"
"   ``https://<your-odoo>/telegram/webhook/<bot_token>`` with Telegram, passing\n"
"   that secret as ``secret_token``. Without a secret the bot token in the\n"
"   webhook URL is the only credential, and that URL is written verbatim to\n"
"   every proxy access log the request passes through; anyone who can read one\n"
"   can post forged updates.\n"
"4. A bot that existed before secrets were enforced is flagged\n"
"   ``legacy_secretless_webhook`` and its updates are still accepted without\n"
"   one (the form warns about it). Register Webhook gives it a secret and ends\n"
"   that.\n"
"5. Add the commands the bot should answer under Telegram > Configuration >\n"
"   Commands and link them on the bot. A handler registered in Python that is not\n"
"   linked to the bot answers \"comando desconocido\".\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"This is a base module that other ``telegram_bot_*`` modules depend on to add\n"
"domain-specific functionality (attendance, approval automation, financial\n"
"reports, project tasks).\n"
"\n"
"Send a message programmatically:\n"
"\n"
".. code-block:: python\n"
"\n"
"    bot = env['telegram.bot'].search([('name', '=', 'My Bot')], limit=1)\n"
"    bot.send_message(chat_id='123456', text='Hello from Odoo!')\n"
"\n"
"Pass ``parse_mode=None`` for text built from untrusted values, or run the values\n"
"through the Markdown helpers:\n"
"\n"
".. code-block:: python\n"
"\n"
"    md = bot.get_markdown_helpers()\n"
"    bot.send_message(chat.chat_id, f\"Hola {md['bold'](partner.name)}\")\n"
"\n"
"Extend with custom commands in a child module:\n"
"\n"
".. code-block:: python\n"
"\n"
"    from odoo.addons.telegram_bot.controllers.telegram_controller import (\n"
"        TelegramController,\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"    class MyBotController(TelegramController):\n"
"        def __init__(self):\n"
"            super().__init__()\n"
"            self._command_handlers['/status'] = '_handle_status_command'\n"
"            self._partner_added_cmds.add('/status')\n"
"\n"
"        def _handle_status_command(self, bot, chat, args, partner=False, internal_user=False):\n"
"            bot.send_message(chat.chat_id, f'Hello {partner.name}!')\n"
"\n"
"Writing a handler\n"
"=================\n"
"\n"
"A handler runs inside a savepoint. If it raises, its database work is rolled\n"
"back, the conversation is reset to ``idle`` and the user is told — so a crash\n"
"cannot strand someone mid-flow.\n"
"\n"
"What is *not* rolled back is anything already sent to Telegram. Odoo re-runs a\n"
"whole endpoint on a serialisation conflict, so keep the outbound calls to the\n"
"model's methods (``send_message``, ``send_document``, ``get_file_content`` …):\n"
"they go through the replay guard and a re-run reuses the first answer. A raw\n"
"``requests`` call from a handler will happen once per attempt.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on GitHub Issues. In case of trouble, please check there\n"
"if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin\n"
msgstr ""

